      "page_title": "Cluster Time & Two-Phase Commit",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Cluster Time",
          "items": [
            "Nodes gossip `$clusterTime` on every message",
            "It is signed, so a client cannot forge a future time",
            "That signature is why you cannot skip replication waits"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Cheaper than a transaction",
          "text": "Transactions are causally consistent by construction. If you only need ordering and not atomicity, a causal session costs far less — just some read latency waiting for replication."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Spanning Shards",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Since 4.2 one transaction can touch multiple shards",
            "`mongos` coordinates the whole thing for the client",
            "A single-shard txn skips coordination entirely"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two-Phase Commit"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "mongos",
              "elect coordinator",
              "send prepare",
              "collect votes",
              "commit or abort"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One participating shard is elected transaction coordinator",
            "Prepared shards write a prepare oplog entry",
            "The decision is durable in `config.transaction_coordinators`",
            "Only then does each shard actually commit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cost Model"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Shards",
            "Path",
            "Cost"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1",
              "no 2PC",
              "≈ replica set txn"
            ],
            [
              "2",
              "full 2PC",
              "prepare + decide"
            ],
            [
              "N",
              "full 2PC",
              "grows with N"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Shard key is the lever",
          "text": "Co-locate documents that must change together — same shard key prefix — and the transaction stays single-shard. That is the whole performance story."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Constraints"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "readConcern must be snapshot, or majority/local",
            "`snapshot` uses a global cluster-wide timestamp",
            "`readPreference` secondary is not allowed",
            "A shard cannot join the transaction once commit begins"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Fighting The Balancer"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A chunk migration conflicting with an in-flight txn aborts it",
            "In-progress prepared txns block chunk migration",
            "They also block some DDL until they resolve"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Coordinator Recovery & Causal Guarantees",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Killed mongos",
          "text": "The coordinator finishes the job without it. The client gets UnknownTransactionCommitResult and must retry commitTransaction — not the whole transaction."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Four Causal Guarantees",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Read your own writes== — even from a secondary",
            "Monotonic reads — never step back in time",
            "Monotonic writes — applied in issue order",
            "Writes follow reads — a write lands after what it read"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// service A → service B",
            "const t = sA.operationTime",
            "const c = sA.clusterTime",
            "sB.advanceClusterTime(c)",
            "sB.advanceOperationTime(t)"
          ],
          "note": "one session only, unless you propagate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Error Labels, Retries & Time Limits",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.serverStatus().transactions.totalPrepared",
            "db.serverStatus()",
            "  .twoPhaseCommitCoordinator",
            "// watch these before blaming the network"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Design Checklist",
          "items": [
            "Keep the txn on one shard where you can",
            "Never span shards for a bulk job",
            "Measure participating shard count, not just latency"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Labels Drive Everything",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Error label",
            "Retry what"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "TransientTransactionError",
              "whole transaction"
            ],
            [
              "UnknownTransactionCommitResult",
              "commitTransaction only"
            ],
            [
              "neither label",
              "fail, do not retry"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Transient covers write conflict, stepdown, NoSuchTransaction",
            "It means nothing applied — safe to run from the beginning",
            "Unknown-commit means the commit may or may not have landed"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "if (e.hasErrorLabel(",
            "  'UnknownTransactionCommitResult')) {",
            "  await session.commitTransaction()  // again",
            "}  // txnNumber makes this idempotent"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Let the driver do it",
          "text": "`withTransaction` implements both loops correctly. Hand-rolled retries almost always get the commit-unknown case wrong."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Time Limits"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Limit",
            "Default",
            "Bounds"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "transactionLifetimeLimitSeconds",
              "60",
              "snapshot age"
            ],
            [
              "maxCommitTimeMS",
              "unset",
              "the commit"
            ],
            [
              "maxTimeMS",
              "unset",
              "one operation"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A periodic cleanup thread kills transactions past the lifetime",
            "You get `Transaction with { txnNumber } has been aborted`",
            "The fix is a smaller transaction, not a bigger limit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Killed From Outside"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Automatic abort on primary stepdown or election",
            "Automatic abort when the session is reaped",
            "Manual: `killSessions`, or `killOp` on the txn's opid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Keep The Snapshot Young",
          "items": [
            "No network calls between start and commit",
            "No user input, no long computation",
            "The snapshot ages the entire time you wait"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Idempotency detail",
          "text": "Because the callback re-runs, generate ObjectIds OUTSIDE it. Otherwise a retry writes a different `_id` than the attempt you thought failed."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Size Limits & Alternatives to Transactions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Size Limits"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Pre-4.2 the total writes had to fit one 16 MB oplog entry",
            "4.2+ splits the transaction into multiple oplog entries",
            "The 16 MB cap on an individual document still stands"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Rules",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Model to avoid them — embed, or accept eventual consistency",
            "Keep them short — under 1000 docs, well under 60 seconds",
            "Keep them narrow — fewer collections, fewer shards, fewer conflicts"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Index the filters",
          "text": "Index every field the transaction filters on. A collection scan inside a transaction holds the snapshot open far longer than the work deserves."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reach For These First"
        },
        {
