        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Optimistic Concurrency"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const r = await c.updateOne(",
            "  { _id, version: v },",
            "  { $set: doc, $inc: { version: 1 } })",
            "if (r.modifiedCount === 0) retry()  // lost race"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A version field plus a filter — no snapshot held open",
            "Zero `modifiedCount` means someone else won the race",
            "Cheapest fix when only one document has to change"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Bounded Retries"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Swallowing errors in the callback — the driver cannot retry",
            "Side effects in the callback — they repeat on every retry",
            "Unbounded manual loops — `withTransaction` stops at **120s**"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Callback runs N times",
          "text": "Treat the `withTransaction` callback as ==re-runnable==: database work only, no emails, no HTTP calls."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Outbox, Hot Documents & Common Mistakes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Outbox Pattern"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "await orders.insertOne(o, { session })",
            "await outbox.insertOne(evt, { session })",
            "// worker drains outbox, publishes later"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "State change and its event land in one write scope",
            "A worker republishes until the consumer acknowledges",
            "Delivery becomes at-least-once, so consumers stay idempotent"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Choosing The Tool"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Situation",
            "Reach for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "one document",
              "$inc / $set"
            ],
            [
              "read-modify-write",
              "findAndModify"
            ],
            [
              "lost-update risk",
              "version filter"
            ],
            [
              "cross-service",
              "outbox"
            ],
            [
              "truly multi-doc",
              "transaction"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Avoid the hot document",
          "text": "One global stats document updated by every order serializes the whole system. Shard the counter across buckets, or aggregate it offline."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Bucketed Counter"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const b = Math.floor(",
            "  Math.random() * 16)",
            "await stats.updateOne(",
            "  { _id: `orders:${b}` },",
            "  { $inc: { n: 1 } }, { session })"
          ],
          "note": "read = sum of all buckets"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "16 buckets spread writes — far fewer ==WriteConflict== aborts",
            "Reads aggregate the buckets with a `$group` sum",
            "Outside a txn, plain `$inc` needs no bucketing at all"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Five Common Mistakes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Missing `{ session }` on one op — it commits and never rolls back",
            "Hand-rolled retry replaying a commit-unknown error twice",
            "Implicit collection creation inside a txn on pre-4.4 servers",
            "Skipping `endSession`, exhausting the server session pool",
            "Assuming serializability — it is snapshot, so write skew bites"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two More Traps"
        }
      ]
