        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Shape That Works"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "await session.withTransaction(async () => {",
            "  await a.updateOne(q, u, { session })",
            "  await b.insertOne(doc, { session })",
            "}, { readConcern, writeConcern })"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Read the label, not the message",
          "text": "Branch on the error label before anything else. It alone tells you whether to replay the whole transaction or only retry the commit."
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "What does a transaction actually cost?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Single-shard: about a normal write plus one commit round-trip",
            "Multi-shard: that, multiplied by prepare and decide phases",
            "Contention cost dwarfs both once a hot document appears"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Guarding Write Skew"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Two txns read the same invariant, write **different** docs",
            "Force a shared write target so the conflict is detected",
            "Or encode the rule as a ==unique index== constraint"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Escape Hatch, Not Default"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "If most operations need a txn, the schema is relational-shaped",
            "Embedding related data makes atomicity free",
            "Document-level atomicity already covers roughly 90% of cases"
          ]
        },
